course: dictionary
lesson: 6674
title: Health words in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are about health, and the clues around them tell you what they mean. «A weight problem» usually means obesity, being very overweight. The word weight is a clue, and so is problem, which tells you something about health is not right.
explain: Science and health lessons use obesity when they talk about food and exercise. Look for the words around it: balanced food, being active and prevent. These clues show that obesity is a health problem, and that eating well and being active can help stop it.
explain: Obesity is about the body, but it is also about feelings. Some people feel hurt or embarrassed when others talk about weight. So when you read or talk about it, use kind words, and remember that people's bodies are different.
fact: Obesity means having much more body fat than is healthy.
fact: Obesity can lead to illnesses such as diabetes and heart disease.
fact: Balanced food and being active help prevent obesity.
fact: Many things affect a person's weight, so it is kind not to judge.
fact: Obesity is an uncountable noun, so we say «obesity», not «an obesity».
exercise: What does obesity mean? | Being very tall for your age | *Having much more body fat than is healthy | Feeling tired after school | Having very long legs
exercise: Which illnesses can obesity lead to? | Growing new teeth | Learning to swim | *Diabetes and heart disease | Better sleep
exercise: Which of these helps prevent obesity? | Sitting still all day | *Eating balanced food and being active | Eating only sweets | Skipping every meal
test: Health reports talk about childhood ___ as a problem. | *Obesity | Weather | Holidays | Sunshine
test: Why should we talk about obesity kindly? | Because it is never a health issue | Because it is a joke | Because only adults can talk about it | *Because bodies differ and many things affect weight
exam: Which sentence uses obesity correctly? | We had an obesity for lunch. | *Scientists say balanced food and exercise help prevent obesity. | Obesity is a colour of the sky. | Lots of sport and fresh food help prevent obesity.
